          November, with iFIT Pro at $39 a month on top for the guided
          content. The Aviron and Sunny in this roundup sit inside that range.
          For every machine ranked purely by maximum grade, including the
          30% TRUE Alpine Runner, see our list of the
          <a href="/treadmills-with-the-highest-incline/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmills with the highest incline</a>,
          and for the dedicated machines on their own, the
          <a href="/best-incline-trainers/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best incline trainers</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Two checks apply to every machine past 20%. First, read the speed
          limit at the top grade, not just the headline top speed: the Aviron
          Summit's Amazon listing gives 14 mph up to a 15% grade, 8 mph
          through 25% and 6 mph above that, and the Sunny tops out at 5 mph
          at any grade. Second, measure your ceiling with the deck at full
          incline, because the front of a long deck rises a long way at 40%,
          and Aviron recommends an 8 ft ceiling for the Summit.
        </p>
